# Sentinel daily brief — crontab alternative for systems without systemd.
#
# Prefer the systemd timer if you have one (deploy/sentinel-daily.timer). It
# handles GMT/BST automatically and catches up after downtime; the two lines
# below can do neither.
#
# Install with:  crontab -e
#
# CRON_TZ makes the schedule follow UK local time including the clock changes.
# Without it, cron uses the system timezone and the brief silently shifts by an
# hour twice a year. Supported by cronie and Vixie cron; NOT by busybox crond,
# where you must set the whole machine's TZ instead.
CRON_TZ=Europe/London

# cron runs with a near-empty environment. The script resolves uv itself, but
# give it a sane PATH anyway.
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
SENTINEL_HOME=/home/YOUR_USER/sentinel
# SENTINEL_UNIVERSE=uk-large

# 07:00, Monday to Friday. Weekends are omitted deliberately: EOD vendors
# publish nothing then, so a weekend run mails you Friday's brief again.
0 7 * * 1-5 /home/YOUR_USER/sentinel/deploy/sentinel-daily.sh >/dev/null 2>&1

# The script logs to $SENTINEL_HOME/logs and pushes an alert on failure, so
# there is nothing useful in cron's own mail. If you would rather have it,
# drop the redirection above and set MAILTO.
